<title>UK: IBCA rates Sal. Oppenheim A long-term.</title>
<headline>IBCA rates Sal. Oppenheim A long-term.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, said on Thursday, it asssigned a long-term rating of A to Sal. Oppenheim Jr. &amp; Cie (Sal. Oppenheim).</p>
<p>&quot;Its short-term rating of A1 remains unchanged,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agency said Sal. Oppenheim, based in Cologne, was Germany's largest unquoted private bank. Its largest subsidiary, the mortgage bank Rheinboden Hypothekenbank, accounted for over half of the group's assets.</p>
<p>&quot;The bank is well capitalised with a very liquid balance sheet. Although its profitability is not as high as that of some of its international peers, it has generally been consistent,&quot; IBCA said.</p>
<p>--International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 4041</p>
</text>
